  "id": "sudden-infant-death-syndrome",
  "term": "sudden infant death syndrome",
  "definition": "Sudden infant death syndrome is the sudden death of an infant during sleep that is linked in this source to a failure to arouse and respond to life-threatening events such as low oxygen. The packet describes it as involving abnormalities in brainstem homeostatic systems, especially medullary pathways that help control breathing, cardiovascular function, and autonomic responses.",
